## Context

Child of 0754. #6012's pinned embeddingsTest.js tests phase ordering,
smallest-first attachment processing, skipping current embeddings, engine
release under memory pressure and the batch-shrinking floor. These mechanisms
serve different components; parity means proving applicable user guarantees,
not copying mechanisms into an extraction-only plugin.

Read: plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js (blocked, workerBusy, list),
scheduler.js, tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs and bootstrap tests, and their
mutation probes. The current sitter enumerates by item ID. SPEC.md §5.2.3
rejects smallest-first for the search pipeline; SPEC.md §5.2.7 owns the sitter
admission and lifecycle contract. 0752 already owns notification coalescing and
reconciliation races.

## Work and exit criteria

- [ ] Map upstream scheduling/resource assertions to the owner and existing
      local evidence. Classify model shutdown and adaptive inference batches
      as consumer work for 0754 to route, not sitter features.
- [ ] Test production admission code as resources change between documents,
      while asynchronous checks run and across off/on or disable/re-enable.
      Cover unreadable/non-finite resource reports and native queue changes.
      Threshold values must resolve to their SPEC owner, not new ticket rules.
- [ ] Prove refusal admits nothing, clears without losing eligible work, and
      never multiplies unresolved submissions. Preserve settlement reporting
      for admitted work after the switch turns off.
- [ ] Test current-pack skipping at the production inspection boundary.
      Keep priority/queue order distinct from the single-admission guarantee;
      expose ordering differences without silently adopting smallest-first.
- [ ] Reuse 0752's implemented coalesced notifications and reconciliation
      tests; inspect the merged code and evidence before identifying gaps.
      Existing admission tests can be strengthened independently.
- [ ] Use behavioral controls or mutation probes that break each newly covered
      safeguard. Record surviving mutations as uncovered guarantees, not passes.
- [ ] Commit evidence under verification/ and bench/results/ with host and code
      identity. Separate deterministic admission guarantees from unmeasured
      peak-memory control, preemption and foreground responsiveness.
- [ ] Update 0754's matrix and make check passes.

This work does not add resource enforcement to the shared native worker.
